Sorry Chris;
Everything has changed. You can join the whiners or you can help our new President Trump's efforts to make our country more competitive in the world. You can jump on the bandwagon to "Make America Great Again"  or you can be left in the dustbin of history. We are going forward with or without you and it would be better for us all if we did this together.
Good luck either path you choose. My hope is for all Americans to prosper and hold their heads high.

You are correct. The definition of sexual assault starts with the definition of common assault :

265 (1) A person commits an assault when
(a) without the consent of another person, he applies force intentionally to that other person, directly or indirectly;
(b) he attempts or threatens, by an act or a gesture, to apply force to another person, if he has, or causes that other person to believe on reasonable grounds that he has, present ability to effect his purpose; 
(2) This section applies to all forms of assault, including sexual assault, sexual assault with a weapon, threats to a third party or causing bodily harm and aggravated sexual assault.

and adds "for a sexual purpose". Basically if you touch or attempt to touch another person for a sexual purpose without their consent, that is sexual assault. Almost every adult has, technically, been sexually assaulted at least once.
